from lb import e
E=[
e("Book 1 - Summary (Jason's arrival to Farrah's death)",["Book 1","Vane Manor","Blood Cult","Greenstone arc","Farrah's death","automaton ambush"],
"""BOOK 1 (Pallimustus, first ~4 months): Jason Asano, a ~23-year-old Australian retail middle manager, wakes naked and hairless in the hedge maze of Vane Estate (Vane Manor) on Pallimustus with a System-like interface (quests, inventory, character sheet) and a World-Phoenix Token. He kills Landemere Vane, absorbs Dark Essence, and frees/joins Rufus Remore, Gary (Gareth Xandier), Farrah Hurin and (briefly) Anisa Lasalle, captives of the Vane family Blood Cult (a Red Table branch). Together they kill the cult (Cressida Vane, Alicia, Darryl Caruthers) and a Sanguine Horror; Jason gains Blood, Sin and Doom essences (Doom is the confluence of Dark+Blood+Sin) and reaches Iron rank. Anisa is fired after killing a traitor contact and trying to kill Colin. Jason goes to Greenstone, meets Danielle and Humphrey Geller, Gabrielle Pellin, Clive Standish, Jory Tillman, Sophie Wexler and Belinda Callahan, learns the Way of the Reaper, passes the Adventure Society field assessment and rises to three stars. He clashes with Thadwick Mercer, crime lords Ventress/Silva/Dorgan and Magic Society director Lucian Lamprey, and sees the Healer and Dominion judge the Church of the Healer. In an astral-space expedition against automaton masters, Farrah Hurin is killed (month 4) and Henry Geller dies; Emir Bahadir arrives to help. The book ends with the expedition aftermath, the trek to Boko and Rufus's grief.""",1),
e("Jason Asano",["Jason","Jason Asano","Asano","Hegemon","Rakishly Handsome Jason","Mr Asano"],
"""Jason Asano (born on Earth, Australia; ~23 at arrival, 44 by Book 12). Former middle manager at an office-supply/retail business who dropped out of political science and lived in Melbourne; irreverent, rambling, pop-culture-quoting joker with a strong moral core, self-doubt and a habit of acting the villain. Arrives on Pallimustus bald with no body hair, speaking all languages via Mysterious Stranger. Mixed Japanese-Australian: father Ken Asano (Japan-born landscape architect), mother Cheryl (Japan-obsessed), older sister Erika (daughter Emi), brother Kaito (Mum's favoured son; married Jason's ex-girlfriend). Four essences absorbed in Book 1: Dark (Speed), Blood (Power), Sin (Recovery), Doom confluence (Spirit) - an 'affliction specialist' build. Early abilities: Midnight Eyes, Cloak of Night, Path of Shadows, Blood Harvest, Leech Bite, Feast of Blood, Sanguine Horror (Colin), Punish, Feast of Absolution, Sin Eater, Hegemony, Inexorable Doom, Punition, Blade of Doom, Verdict, Castigate, Haemorrhage. Fights with the Way of the Reaper martial art, Dread Salvation sword (from Gary), Night Fang dagger and a Trap Weaver Battle Robe. Immune to tracking/identification. See later entries for his growth: Bronze, Silver, the Hegemon, Prime Avatar and System Administrator.""",1),
e("Rufus Remore",["Rufus","Remore","Rufus Remore"],
"""Rufus Remore: tall, bald, handsome Black man from Vitesse (voice 'like dark chocolate'), grandson of diamond-ranker Roland Remore (chancellor of Remore Academy); father Gabriel Remore, mother Arabelle. Leader/guide of Jason's first adventuring group, fencer-type (scimitar of golden light, silver swords, water-walking boots, speed/time-freeze ability). Moral anchor: told Jason on his first night what an adventurer is - someone who stands between the bad things and those who need protecting; rule 'personal possessions only' when looting. Guilt-stricken after Farrah dies ('she followed me'). Childhood friend of the Crown Princess of Vitesse. Mentor-like friend of Emir Bahadir. Later a major gold-rank force on Earth beside Taika.""",1),
e("Gary (Gareth Xandier) - original",["Gary","Gareth Xandier","Gareth","leonid Gary","Gary Xandier","original Gary"],
"""Gareth 'Gary' Xandier: huge leonid (lion-headed, growly) crafter-warrior with forge/iron powers: conjured dark runed steel armour, hammer and shield, a foundry golem summon (from iron filings). Rufus's friend; deeply loyal and practical; makes Jason's sword Dread Salvation ('first and last gift'). Dominion notes him ('Gareth Xandier... that is where monarchs come from'). In Book 10 he drinks the Cup of Heroes and becomes a demigod; in Book 11 he refuses a natural-array alternative, dies ~1 year later and is reincarnated as a baby leonid; by Book 12 he is a teenage leonid, 'Gary Sharpton'. Jason calls him 'brother'.""",1),
e("Farrah Hurin",["Farrah","Hurin","Huren","Farrah Hurin","Defier of the Will"],
"""Farrah Hurin: small, pale, strawberry-blonde with a button nose and a savage, wise temperament; Vitesse-born ritual magician and Magic Society member (parents Amelia and William Hurin). Essences Earth, Fire, Potent -> Volcano confluence: Lava Cannon, Magma Golem (obsidian powder), Flamecore Ravager, Magma Trap, Volcanic Resurgence. Teaches Jason aura control, perception, meditation and ritual circles (taught the summoning circle for Colin). DIES in Book 1 (month 4, automaton ambush: four metal arms of a silver abomination pierce body and head); funeral month 5. Revived and found on Earth in Book 4 (as a second outworlder), reaches silver and gold; in Book 12 chooses to become an immortal Defier of the Will. Confidante of Jason; co-founder with Travis Noble of the Sky Link Company.""",1),
e("Anisa Lasalle",["Anisa","Lasalle","Purity priestess"],
"""Anisa Lasalle: platinum-blonde elf, healer-priestess of Purity (her church wanted the Vane estate), spell Regenerate ('Let the life that has withered return to full bloom'). Initially on Rufus's team; kills the traitor contact in a desert cabin before he can talk and tries to kill Colin as 'tainted'. Rufus fires her; she takes the wagon and animals and calls humans 'filth'. Cassandra Mercer later learns she belongs to the Lasalle family.""",1),
e("Vane Family (Blood Cult) and Vane Estate",["Vane","Vane Estate","Vane Manor","Landemere","Cressida","Alicia Vane","Darryl Caruthers","Dougall","Blood Cult"],
"""Vane Estate/Vane Manor: lush estate in a Kalahari-like region (two moons overhead) with climate-pillar magic, hedge maze, well and subterranean ritual chamber; seat of a Blood Cult branch of the Red Table. Lady Cressida Vane (matriarch), son Landemere Vane (Builder cultist, astral specialist; tried to summon an astral being and pulled Jason across; killed by Jason's Seal Knife; familiar Umbral Mountain Snake), daughter Alicia Vane (killed by Gary's trowel), Cressida's husband Darryl Caruthers (high priest), and servant Dougall (cannibal with shovel). They were building a Sanguine Horror. Jason kills most of them; Cressida and Darryl die after he shoves them into stone. The Adventure Society later names a conference room the 'Edith Vane Memorial'.""",1),
e("Sanguine Horror / Colin",["Sanguine Horror","Colin","apocalypse beast"],
"""Sanguine Horror: an apocalypse beast of carrion/lamprey leeches in blood-soaked bandages; regenerates from a single leech; weak to salt and lava (weaknesses fade by gold rank). Jason's Awakening Stone of the Apocalypse gives the Sanguine Horror familiar ability; he names it COLIN ('Team Colin'): a leech on his shoulder that communicates left=yes/right=no, melts into blood to heal him, swarm form, 'worm-that-walks' form (bronze), blood robes (silver), gold: can exceed mass limits via life drain. Summoned familiars can vanish into the summoner and die with them; bonded familiars survive their owner but cannot vanish. At diamond Colin reaches full sanguine-horror strength.""",1),
e("Greenstone",["Greenstone","Old City","The Island","Mistrun Delta","Geller estate"],
"""Greenstone: coastal city on the Mistrun River delta in a low-magic desert region (exports green marble and lesser spirit coins). Split into the Old City (red-yellow 12m walls, harbour) and The Island (rich district/breakwater of green marble reached by four bridges with a permit system). Magic trams run through water tunnels. Divine Square holds temples of Dominion, Journey/Roads, Knowledge, Healer. Fortress (neutral crime-lord ground with pit fights), Cavendish district, Broadstreet Clinic (Jory), Sailor's Watch inn (Madam Landry/Jessica), Adventure Society hall and trade hall, Magic Society (Lucian Lamprey, Clive), Geller estate. Nominally ruled by the Duke of Greenstone. Monster surge every ~10 years. Later hosts the Geller-Remore training facility.""",1),
e("Geller Family",["Geller","Gellers","Geller estate","Geller compound"],
"""The Gellers: a large, tough, honour-bound adventuring clan (broad shoulders, chiselled features) from Greenstone who deliberately train in low-magic conditions. Members include Danielle (matriarch/strategist), Humphrey, Rick, Phoebe, Jonah, Henry (died Book 1), Henrietta, Valdis. Operate the Geller-Seven spirit coin farm; a diamond-rank ancestor is rumoured. Later partner with Remore Academy (Geller-Remore facility).""",1),
e("Danielle Geller",["Danielle","Danielle Geller","Geller matriarch"],
"""Danielle Geller: looks ~30, actually ~50, silver-ranker (time-confluence essence; dimensional blade, acceleration, damage reflection) and Humphrey's mother; diplomat/strategist who becomes Jason's adviser on etiquette and politics (hired as political advisor in Book 12). Investigated Jason for Gabriel Remore; fought in the ambush where Farrah died.""",1),
e("Humphrey Geller",["Humphrey","Humphrey Geller","Hump"],
"""Humphrey Geller: tall, broad, handsome Geller who becomes leader of Jason's team (Team Biscuit). Dragon-confluence essence: dragon wings, rainbow-scale armour, dragon-wing sword and angel-feather sword, fire breath, Spartoi dragon-tooth warriors, Dragon Might aura, Dive Bomb, Unstoppable Force, later Mighty Strength and Immortality; familiar Stash (Velitraxistaasch, shapeshifting dragon: puppy/canary/hill mouse/rainbow dragon). Failed Rufus's field assessment first (boldness); Hero's Drive racial gift. Early romance with Gabrielle Pellin. Likes Jason's biscuits. In Book 1 confronts Jason over mirage-arena cruelty.""",1),
e("Gabrielle Pellin",["Gabrielle","Gabrielle Pellin","Gabby","Knowledge acolyte"],
"""Gabrielle Pellin: acolyte, later priestess, of Knowledge; blue-and-white robes, might essence, conjured iron staff. Initially disapproves of Jason ('dangerous ideas'); her goddess takes interest in him. Humphrey's early girlfriend; later married to Travis Noble. Jason apologises to her in Book 12.""",1),
e("Sophie Wexler",["Sophie","Sophie Wexler","The Nightingale","Nightingale"],
"""Sophie Wexler 'the Nightingale': celestine woman (chocolate skin, silver hair and eyes). Arrived as a toddler with her father (muscle for a merchant group); he worked for Silva; after his failed expedition she was indentured with huge debt and fought in Fortress pits, then became a thief with Belinda Callahan. Speed essence (wall/water running, later Eternal Moment time acceleration). Sheltered by Clarissa Ventress, hunted by Cole Silva and Lucian Lamprey. Jason claims her via the right of first refusal (Book 1-2) and she joins his team. Fights in her father's Way-of-the-Reaper style. Later she and Humphrey become a couple (engaged by Book 11). Her indentured past drives her fierce support of Jason's anti-slavery System shutdown in Book 12.""",1),
e("Belinda Callahan",["Belinda","Lindy","Belinda Callahan"],
"""Belinda 'Lindy' Callahan: short scraggly-haired human, Sophie's friend, planner and tool-maker thief turned adventurer. Later powers: Instant Adept (temporary roles via item sets), Force Tether, Mirror Magic (copies and double-casts Farrah's/Clive's spells), scout/tracker. Courted by Jory Tillman. Team Biscuit's tactician and gadgeteer; helps abduct Cyrion nobles in Book 12.""",1),
e("Clive Standish",["Clive","Clive Standish","Magister"],
"""Clive Standish: tall lanky scholar from an eel farm, Magic Society researcher with rune-based essences (circles, Rune Trap, Mantle of Retribution, Wrath of the Magister, Mana Equilibrium). Familiar Onslow, a rune tortoise (flying battle platform later). Venerates the Celestial Book. Astral-magic expert; explains the cosmos to Jason as 'dumpling soup'. Becomes founder/Archchancellor of the Magic Research Association (Book 12) and co-inventor of the sky link. Unmarried: the 'imaginary wife' is a running gag in the series; by Book 13 his partner is Lorelei Grantham.""",1),
e("Jory Tillman",["Jory","Jory Tillman","Broadstreet Clinic"],
"""Jory Tillman: iron-rank alchemist-adventurer with the Broadstreet Clinic in Greenstone Old City; sells cheap potions, crystal wash and 'Togetherness Jelly'. Jason invests 3 gold coins in him. Smitten with Belinda. By Book 12 a leading alchemist who travels to Earth. The Church of the Healer once branded him heretic; the Healer blesses his clinic.""",1),
e("Neil Davone",["Neil","Neil Davone","Healer priest"],
"""Neil Davone: healer-adventurer who stands with Jory against the Healer's priests; joins the Church of the Healer's penitents and becomes a priest of the Healer; later Team Biscuit's body healer (Grand Renewal, summons, buffs). Serves Thadwick Mercer in Book 1 before quitting. Jason's friend/foil; Cassandra Mercer's ex.""",1),
e("Mercer Family (Thalia, Thadwick, Cassandra)",["Mercer","Thalia Mercer","Thadwick","Thadwick Mercer","Cassandra","Cassandra Mercer","Beaufort Mercer"],
"""Mercer family of Greenstone Island: Lady Thalia Mercer (silver adventurer-turned-noble, wants Cassandra to wed Rufus), husband Beaufort Mercer, son Thadwick Mercer (storm/lightning-potent essences; incompetent, cheats the assessment system, land-grab scheme with summoned fergax; flees the ambush leaving allies) and daughter Cassandra Mercer (olive skin, dark hair, hidden aura; clever; one-night stand with Jason; later Neil's ex; reaches silver). Thalia is the Duke of Greenstone's sister-in-law.""",1),
e("Elspeth Arella and Adventure Society Greenstone",["Elspeth Arella","Arella","Greenstone branch director","Vincent Trenslow","Genevieve Picot","Guy Spalding","Albert Bertinelli","Berts"],
"""Elspeth Arella: elf, silver, Director of the Greenstone Adventure Society branch; rose from poverty; daughter of crime lord Adris Dorgan (hidden); scheming but reformist; aims to oust Lucian Lamprey; promotes Jason to 3 stars. Staff: Vincent Trenslow (waxed twirled moustache, strict instructor), Genevieve Picot (deputy director), Guy Spalding (corrupt official tied to Silva), Albert Bertinelli (clerk; one of the 'Berts' octuplets: Bertram, Herbert, Robert, Gilbert, Filbert, Hubert, Bertrand).""",1),
e("Greenstone Crime Lords (Big Three) and Fortress",["Clarissa Ventress","Ventress","Cole Silva","Silva","Adris Dorgan","Dorgan","Fortress","Big Three","Lucian Lamprey","Pochard Finn"],
"""Big Three of Greenstone's underworld: Clarissa Ventress (ambitious, canal-district mansion; shelters Sophie as bait against Silva), Cole Silva (impetuous, obsessed with Sophie) and Adris Dorgan (elf, bronze, 'the quiet one', Elspeth Arella's father). The Fortress is an ancient warehouse-district stone arena/neutral ground. Lucian Lamprey (muscular elf, Magic Society Greenstone director, banished there) rents a box and is obsessed with the Nightingale; his deputy Pochard Finn is Clive's boss.""",1),
e("Way of the Reaper (martial art)",["Way of the Reaper","Five Forms","Reaper skill book","Hierophant","Trickster","Hermit","Hunter","Sage"],
"""Way of the Reaper: legendary iron skill book found by Rufus's team under a lake (two crossed scythes over a skull). Five forms: Sage (mobile, vs many/limbed enemies), Hierophant (direct, aggressive), Trickster (drunken-boxing style), Hunter (debilitating attacks on the unaware, find weak points), Hermit (counters/defence vs humans and bizarre monsters). Key skill is transitions between forms. Jason learns it in Book 1; Clive finds copies in an ancient Order of the Reaper complex under Greenstone (Forms One and Three). Sophie's father also used it. Emir Bahadir investigates the Order of the Reaper (ancient assassin order).""",1),
e("Dread Salvation",["Dread Salvation","Jason's sword","Gary's sword"],
"""Dread Salvation: iron legendary growth sword made by Gary for Jason (red-gold hilt, black tassel). Stacking buffs Stone Cutter (vs physical immunity) and Spell Breaker (vs magical immunity) built from resonating-force damage when immunities trigger. Growth upgrades need huge rare materials. Jason keeps it for life; called 'the first and last gift from Gary' (Book 12).""",1),
e("The Healer, Dominion and Knowledge (Book 1 divine events)",["Healer","Dominion","Knowledge","Hero","Divine Square","Healer's Judgement"],
"""Healer's Judgement (Greenstone): when the Chief Priest of the Healer marches on Jory's Broadstreet Clinic, the god Healer appears (small, middle-aged, plain brown robes), regrows a foot, strips corrupt clergy of their essences and welcomes Neil; Dominion (young, handsome, crowned, cruel-eyed, fire aura) offers to take the stripped power-seekers; the Healer seals the penitents' returned essences and blesses the clinic. Knowledge (Mediterranean-looking woman) meets Jason in her temple: he was not chosen, the World-Phoenix Token is his way home and will use itself 'when circumstances dictate'. Dominion says of Jason 'I love that guy'.""",1),
e("Automaton Ambush (Desert Astral Space)",["automaton","desert astral space","astral space expedition","Boko","Farrah's funeral"],
"""Book 1 climax: Danielle Geller leads a large Greenstone expedition into the desert astral space (turquoise lagoon, 5-sided engraved columns relaying astral magic) after Ustei nomads flee north. A construct army (wooden puppets, stone golems, clockwork animals, steel spider) led by sandy-robed bronze/silver masters and silver-rank abominations (metal grafted into flesh, four extra metal arms) ambushes them. Farrah Hurin is killed; Henry Geller dies; Jonah and Thadwick+3 are found injured; Rufus loses an arm and is crushed by guilt. Emir's cloud palace and portaler Hester (via Boko) help; two captives suicide by exploding crystals. The network of astral nodes is disrupted. Boko is a dark-skinned human desert city and the mainland base.""",1),
e("Emir Bahadir and Constance",["Emir","Emir Bahadir","Bahadir","Constance","Cloud House","cloud palace"],
"""Emir Bahadir: gold-ranker, midnight-black skin and beaded hair, Rufus's mentor-ally; wealthy Vitesse-based finder of rare items for diamond/gold clients; owns a dimensional-jacket flask holding cloud forms (estate, bus, palace, ship) and a 300m x 60m cloud ship. Wife Constance (silver, pale, brown hair; indispensable). Staff include portaler Hester. In Book 12 supports Jason in Cyrion. Ketis Bahadir is a relative.""",1),
e("Mirage Chamber, Skill Books and Spirit Coins",["mirage chamber","skill book","spirit coin","coins","lesser spirit coin"],
"""Mirage chamber: dome with illusion bodies for safe training (limited by local magic). Skill books impart techniques via a text swarm and must be absorbed while conscious. Spirit coin ladder: 100 lesser = 1 iron; then x10 each: iron -> bronze -> silver -> gold -> diamond (gold coin = 100,000 lesser). Consuming a higher-rank coin temporarily raises attributes to that rank with backlash. Lesser coins are Greenstone's biggest export. Jason's coins carry his thumbs-up face ('PRODUCT OF JASON / G'DAY MATE').""",1),
]
